# Pier pile in swim water (TileKind::Swim, D-076): a 4 px O/l wooden pile
# (cols 6-9, lit left) going down through the clear swim water; used
# under the ends of `steg` decks, whose end tiles carry the same pile.
# Vertical autotile, only N and S matter: with an open top the tile shows
# the tile_see_wasser surface (frame 0) and a w ripple where the pile
# breaks the skin; with swim-pile above it shows tile_see_wasser_tief
# (frame 0); with an open bottom the pile ends in a small i/m gravel heap
# on the lake bed. Static (an autotile has one anim), so it shows the
# water's frame 0.
# Autotiled (D-020): anim `auto`, frame = neighbour mask
# (1 = same tile above, 2 = right, 4 = below, 8 = left; level edge = same).
sprite = tile_steg_pfahl
size   = 16x16
origin = 0,0
anim   = auto frames=16 ticks=1
